From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll/virtual: report why a PS4 reservation was refused

anon_mmap_tryfixed() sets errno = EEXIST whatever sceKernelReserveVirtualRange
answers, so every refusal reached the caller as a collision. A whole day was
spent hunting a squatter at 0x400000 on the strength of an errno we wrote
ourselves, while find_view_range() correctly reported the range free -- it
tracks Wine's views, which never include the host executable.

Log what the kernel was actually asked and what it answered, and query the
range so the owner is named. That single line identified the cause at once:

  PW_RESERVE refused rc=0x8002000c base=400000 want=0x130000 host=0x130000
    prot=0x3; query rc=0 start=400000 end=49c000 qprot=0x5 qflags=0x11
    name=executable hole=0

rc 0x8002000c is errno 12, ENOMEM; name=executable is the title's own eboot.
Fixed properly in prospero-win patch 0201, which restores the eboot release.

Also kept, as defence in depth, both bounded and both no-ops once 0201 lands:

  - ROUND_SIZE on the size passed to the reservation. map_fixed_area() already
    rounds, so this only matters for the call sites that do not (virtual.c
    ~1090, and the DOS-memory ones), and anon_mmap_fixed() asserts the same
    alignment. An earlier package shipped this alone as a fix; it is not one.
  - A query-then-MAP_FIXED fallback when the reservation is refused, used only
    when the query proves the whole request is a hole, and never for PROT_NONE
    so that reserve_area()'s blocks of up to 1.7 GiB cannot consume the
    title's ~440 MiB flexible pool.

Method note: three theories were inferred from logged values and all three were
wrong. The one that worked was printing the failing call's own arguments and
return code. Instrument the call before theorising about it.

---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -974,6 +974,10 @@
 static void *anon_mmap_tryfixed( void *start, size_t size, int prot, int flags )
 {
     void *ptr;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    size_t host_size;
+    int reserve_rc;
+#endif
 
 #ifdef MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE
     ptr = mmap( start, size, prot, MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON | flags, -1, 0 );
@@ -983,18 +987,110 @@
     /* The kernel ignores MAP_EXCL, so claim the range with a reservation
      * that refuses to overwrite, then map over it if needed. */
     ptr = start;
-    if (sceKernelReserveVirtualRange( &ptr, size, PS5_MAP_FIXED | PS5_MAP_NO_OVERWRITE, host_page_size ))
+    /* The reservation is refused outright unless the size is a whole number
+     * of host pages, and the PS4's are 16 KiB while a PE section is only
+     * 4 KiB-aligned -- so an image whose size is not a 16 KiB multiple (e.g.
+     * FalloutNV.exe, 0x1009000) never reserves at its preferred base. The
+     * refusal is then reported to the caller as EEXIST, which reads as a
+     * collision rather than a bad argument, and the range is never handed to
+     * __wine_ps5_dmem_region(), so everything mapped there falls back to the
+     * title's small flexible pool. Round up, as every other host-page path in
+     * this file does; anon_mmap_fixed() asserts the same alignment. */
+    host_size = ROUND_SIZE( start, size, host_page_mask );
+    reserve_rc = sceKernelReserveVirtualRange( &ptr, host_size, PS5_MAP_FIXED | PS5_MAP_NO_OVERWRITE, host_page_size );
+    if (reserve_rc)
     {
-        errno = EEXIST;
-        return MAP_FAILED;
+        /* Measured on FW 12.02 (package 1043): this call returns 0x8002000c
+         * (ENOMEM) for EVERY fixed reservation, down to a 64 KiB PROT_NONE
+         * range -- 54 of 54 in one Fallout launch, none granted. It is the
+         * call, not a shortage: plain mmap succeeds at the same addresses,
+         * which is how FalloutNV.exe loads at 0x530000 after this refuses
+         * 0x400000. Giving up here leaves reserved_areas empty, so
+         * mmap_add_reserved_area() and __wine_ps5_dmem_region() never run,
+         * no range is dmem-backed, and the title exhausts its ~440 MiB
+         * flexible pool in about 3.5 minutes.
+         *
+         * So fall back to what every other port does and the generic branch
+         * of this same function already relies on: map it, then check we got
+         * the address we asked for. The PS4 kernel ignores MAP_EXCL, which is
+         * why the reservation was preferred, but verify-after-map catches the
+         * same case -- a mapping placed elsewhere is unmapped and reported as
+         * EEXIST, exactly as at the top of this function. */
+        /* Only for mappings that are about to be used. reserve_area() asks
+         * for PROT_NONE blocks up to 1.7 GiB to claim address space; if the
+         * PS4 charges flexible memory on mmap regardless of prot, satisfying
+         * those would swallow the whole ~440 MiB pool at startup -- worse
+         * than the refusal. Address-space reservation stays refused; real
+         * mappings (image loads, the case that relocates Fallout and kills
+         * Oblivion) take the fallback. Revisit the PROT_NONE case only after
+         * measuring what a large PROT_NONE mmap costs here. */
+        if (prot == PROT_NONE)
+        {
+            ERR( "PW_RESERVE refused rc=%#x base=%p want=%#zx host=%#zx align=%#zx got=%p prot=none; no fallback\n",
+                 reserve_rc, start, size, host_size, (size_t)host_page_size, ptr );
+            errno = EEXIST;
+            return MAP_FAILED;
+        }
+        {
+            /* 1044 took this fallback and still failed: that mmap passes
+             * start as a HINT, not MAP_FIXED, and the PS4 kernel ignores the
+             * hint -- it returned a different address, so verify-after-map
+             * unmapped it and reported EEXIST. The same reason FalloutNV.exe
+             * lands at 0x530000: the kernel chooses, we do not.
+             *
+             * What the refused reservation provided was "map exactly here,
+             * but only if nothing is there". Rebuild that from a call which
+             * does work on PS4: query the range, and use MAP_FIXED only when
+             * the query proves the whole request is a hole. Requiring the
+             * hole to cover the entire range keeps MAP_FIXED from clobbering
+             * a live mapping if the query is read wrongly. */
+            struct ps4_virtual_query_info
+            {
+                void *start, *end;
+                int64_t offset;
+                int32_t protection, memory_type;
+                uint8_t flags;
+                char name[32];
+            } qi;
+            extern int sceKernelVirtualQuery( const void *, int, void *, size_t );
+            int qrc, hole;
+
+            memset( &qi, 0, sizeof(qi) );
+            qrc = sceKernelVirtualQuery( start, 1, &qi, sizeof(qi) );
+            /* Nothing mapped (query fails), or a described region that is
+             * unprotected, unflagged and spans the whole request. */
+            hole = (qrc != 0) ||
+                   (qi.protection == 0 && qi.flags == 0 &&
+                    (char *)qi.end >= (char *)start + host_size);
+
+            ERR( "PW_RESERVE refused rc=%#x base=%p want=%#zx host=%#zx prot=%#x; "
+                 "query rc=%d start=%p end=%p qprot=%#x qtype=%#x qflags=%#x name=%.31s hole=%d\n",
+                 reserve_rc, start, size, host_size, prot,
+                 qrc, qi.start, qi.end, qi.protection, qi.memory_type,
+                 (unsigned)qi.flags, qi.name, hole );
+
+            if (!hole) { errno = EEXIST; return MAP_FAILED; }
+
+            ptr = mmap( start, host_size, prot,
+                        MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON | MAP_FIXED | flags, -1, 0 );
+            if (ptr == MAP_FAILED) return MAP_FAILED;
+            if (ptr != start)
+            {
+                munmap( ptr, host_size );
+                errno = EEXIST;
+                return MAP_FAILED;
+            }
+            __wine_ps5_dmem_region( start, host_size );
+            return start;
+        }
     }
     /* Protecting a bare reservation does not back it with memory, so a
      * later commit would fault on its first access: direct memory backs
      * this range like the reserved areas (until it is unmapped). */
-    __wine_ps5_dmem_region( start, size );
-    if (prot != PROT_NONE && anon_mmap_fixed( start, size, prot, flags ) == MAP_FAILED)
+    __wine_ps5_dmem_region( start, host_size );
+    if (prot != PROT_NONE && anon_mmap_fixed( start, host_size, prot, flags ) == MAP_FAILED)
     {
-        munmap( start, size );
+        munmap( start, host_size );
         return MAP_FAILED;
     }
 #elif defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__FreeBSD_kernel__)
